& [FeatureFlowchart] is the minimum repeated checkpoint path
  + [F0 Open] host opens one exact context under compact custody
  + [F1 RequestAdvance] host asks model for exactly one advance_attention_procedure call
  + [F2 AdmitCall] host validates closed quota arguments and run phase
  + [F3 Advance] host applies one exact compare-and-set ADVANCE
  + [F4 ProjectReady] paused result becomes one verified ReadyProjection
  + [F5 ContinueInference] separate provider pass receives ordered transcript and projection then returns to F2
  + [F6 ProjectTerminal] terminal result is READ and becomes verified TerminalProjection
  + [F7 Reflect] separate no-tool provider pass imports terminal projection
  + [F8 Complete] final output and complete transcript replay-verify
  + [F9 Stop] any cap refusal or fault seals a stopped report and current reentry handle
  + [path] F0 -> F1 -> F2 -> F3 -> F4 -> F5 -> F2 repeated or F6 -> F7 -> F8
  + [stop_path] any active state -> F9

& [RunPolicy]
  + [IAPL-001] host policy binds positive maximum_steps_per_call maximum_tool_calls maximum_provider_calls and timeout
  + [IAPL-002] parallel tool calls are false and only one run-scoped tool exists
  + [IAPL-003] provider can neither increase policy bounds nor supply registry session sequence record or handle digests
  + [IAPL-004] default policy is deliberately small and caller-visible

& [ReadyProjection]
  + [IAPL-005] derive only from a successful READY compact response and exact successor handle
  + [IAPL-006] carry profile session sequence record digest checkpoint digest handle digest slice progress and next legal operation
  + [IAPL-007] carry no checkpoint body context or model-generated semantic summary
  + [IAPL-008] declare state remains nonterminal and exact state remains under host custody

& [IterationRecord]
  + [IAPL-009] bind zero-based iteration index predecessor handle request sanitized response exact parsed call compact response and ready or terminal projection
  + [IAPL-010] exactly one successor projection exists per admitted iteration
  + [IAPL-011] successor sequence and predecessor digest form a causal chain with no gap or fork
  + [IAPL-012] private reasoning fields are absent recursively

& [ProviderLoop]
  + [IAPL-013] first pass and every READY continuation require exactly one advance call with host-selected quota
  + [IAPL-014] each READY projection is appended as a tool result before a new provider request
  + [IAPL-015] earlier tool calls and results remain ordered but exact context and checkpoint bodies remain absent
  + [IAPL-016] provider final content before terminal is a protocol fault
  + [IAPL-017] terminal state disables tools and uses the P0 verified TerminalProjection reflection contract

& [StopAndReentry]
  + [IAPL-018] tool-call or provider-call cap exhaustion produces stopped not failed or completed state
  + [IAPL-019] stopped report carries exact current compact handle policy usage last verified projection and stop reason
  + [IAPL-020] reentry requires the still-live owning compact process and exact registry digest session sequence and record digest
  + [IAPL-021] process restart makes volatile reentry unavailable and must be reported honestly
  + [IAPL-022] provider schema call compact or projection fault produces faulted stopped report with no invented successor

& [IterativeReport]
  + [IAPL-023] strict report binds policy provider model opening identity ordered iterations exact final observation terminal projection optional final reflection and stopped state
  + [IAPL-024] completed report has terminal projection and final output but no reentry handle
  + [IAPL-025] stopped report has reentry handle but no terminal projection or final output
  + [IAPL-026] exact final record is stored once and never duplicated into model-facing history
  + [IAPL-027] replay reconstructs every request call projection handle transition and terminal reflection without provider or procedure execution

& [FacultyCycle]
  + [IAPL-028] Honesty validates state names completion claims and projection derivation
  + [IAPL-029] Security validates custody compare-and-set identity policy and closed calls
  + [IAPL-030] Planner validates bounds legal next state and stop conditions
  + [IAPL-031] Weaver validates ordered causal transcript and predecessor chain
  + [IAPL-032] Scribe validates exact public record and privacy omission
  + [IAPL-033] Refiner validates minimum sufficient projection and no exact-record duplication
  + [IAPL-034] Observer admits each iteration and final report only after all required checks

& [Boundary]
  + [IAPL-035] provider calls are separate inference checkpoints and not one shared transformer forward pass
  + [IAPL-036] no hidden state KV cache live-token insertion persistent session effect execution or producer authentication is added
  + [IAPL-037] no automatic remote EVO-X2 or OneDrive access is added
  + [IAPL-038] this checkpoint authorizes design planning fixtures and acceptance formation only not implementation

& [Acceptance]
  + [IAPL-A01] quota-eight governed fixture produces at least one READY iteration then byte-identical terminal outcome
  + [IAPL-A02] exact one-call terminal path remains backward-compatible with P0 final identity
  + [IAPL-A03] cap exhaustion yields replay-valid stopped report and live reentry handle
  + [IAPL-A04] wrong call missing call early answer stale handle projection drift transcript fork and restart loss fail closed
  + [IAPL-A05] replay catches mutation of any policy iteration handle projection stop or final field
  + [IAPL-A06] measurement compares repeated model-facing bytes with stateless and one-call baselines
  + [IAPL-A07] implementation requires a separate activation solution proof narrative full regression and publication checkpoint

